I walk to the billing counter.
I have three new garments in my hand.
I am buying a blue kurta, a red t-shirt, and a white scarf.
I put these clothes on the counter.
There is a cashier there.
He prepares the bill.
"The total is exactly one thousand rupees," he says.
I do not use a card.
I take cash from the bag.
I give one thousand rupees to him.
He gives me a large shopping bag.
This shopping bag is very big.
My new clothes are in it.
I will wear the new blue kurta tomorrow.
I will wear the red t-shirt at the gym.
These clothes are very nice.
I take my shopping bag.
I walk out of the shop.
